# Reference sources, fetched 2026-11-06

The C files in this directory are from FreeBSD (`freebsd/freebsd-src`,
branch `main`) and are used as the *behavioural reference* for the D1 ACL
work. They are not compiled or linked into wmng.

Licence: BSD-2-Clause, with the original copyright notices intact in every
file (Chris D. Faulhaber, Robert N. M. Watson, Edward Tomasz Napierła,
TrustedBSD Project).

The wmng source (`src/model.rs`, `src/ops.rs`, the applets and providers)
is a fresh Rust implementation that follows the DESIGN decisions extracted
into ../ACL-PORT-SPEC.md: the option-queue semantics, the merge/remove
algorithms, and the NFSv4 text grammar come from these files; the Win32
DACL handling is ours. Where a behaviour could only be decided by reading
the reference, the spec cites the function that decided it.

